{"seq":1,"slug":"negotiation-theory","title":"谈判理论基础","stage":"DONE","category":"negotiation-communication","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/negotiation-communication/negotiation-theory","rating":{"composite":3.59,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.8,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":3.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.21,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":2.5}},"introMarkdown":"# 谈判理论基础\n\n谈判是人类社会中最古老、最普遍的互动形式之一。无论是薪资协商、商业合作、国际外交还是日常生活中的意见分歧，谈判无处不在。谈判理论基础旨在系统性地梳理谈判学的核心概念框架、经典方法论和前沿策略思维，帮助读者从\"凭直觉谈\"进化为\"有体系地谈\"。\n\n本 Hub 从四个维度展开：首先是谈判学的基础概念，包括谈判的定义与本质、分配式与整合式谈判的区分、以及 BATNA 和 ZOPA 等核心分析工具；其次是哈佛谈判法（原则性谈判），这是全球影响力最大的谈判方法论，源自 Roger Fisher 和 William Ury 的经典著作《Getting to Yes》；第三部分聚焦实战策略，涵盖前 FBI 首席人质谈判专家 Chris Voss 的战术共情方法、锚定效应与框架策略、让步模式与时间策略等；最后从博弈论视角审视谈判中的策略互动，包括合作博弈、重复博弈与声誉机制。\n\n无论你是刚接触谈判的初学者，还是希望系统升级谈判思维的职场人士，这些内容都将为你提供从理论到实践的完整知识地图。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"谈判基础概念","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/negotiation-communication/negotiation-theory/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"negotiation-defined","title":"谈判的定义与本质 Negotiation: Definition and Essence","url":"/l-doc-books/h/negotiation-communication/negotiation-theory/foundations/negotiation-defined"},{"seq":2,"slug":"distributive-integrative","title":"分配式与整合式谈判 Distributive and Integrative Negotiation","url":"/l-doc-books/h/negotiation-communication/negotiation-theory/foundations/distributive-integrative"},{"seq":3,"slug":"batna-zopa","title":"BATNA、ZOPA 与谈判力学 BATNA, ZOPA, and Negotiation Dynamics","url":"/l-doc-books/h/negotiation-communication/negotiation-theory/foundations/batna-zopa"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"harvard-method","title":"哈佛谈判法","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/negotiation-communication/negotiation-theory/harvard-method","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"principled-negotiation","title":"原则性谈判：Getting to Yes Principled Negotiation: Getting to Yes","url":"/l-doc-books/h/negotiation-